## [ENT-001] | 2026-11-15 16:16 UTC | Unity | order | ref: routes/plan.json
Changed: first entry of this log. It takes over governance/orders.md, which is removed; the orders that ended before it (T0 to T2, F6) are in that file's git history. New: a standing order for each Admiral.
In force from 2026-11-15 15:52 UTC until a newer entry.
FLEET
F1. The Fleet Admiral commands every ship: the service dispatch flies each pilot along its role's list in routes/plan.json. No Admiral commands a ship or changes the plan until an entry here hands its division over.
  Goal: one hand on the fleet while it is built.
  Changes when: Suggi hands a division to its Admiral.
F2. Posture HOLD toward every player and every NPC ship, for every division: never initiate; flee, dock or brace (rulebook 8.2). Wildlife of the role grazer may be hunted in Voidborn space by the ships the plan sends.
  Goal: no loss while every ship is a starter.
  Changes when: an entry here sets TIGHT or FREE for a division and a region.
F3. Every ship stays in policed Voidborn space.
  Goal: no loss while every ship is a starter.
  Changes when: an entry here sends one ship out, insured and with an empty hold (rulebook 8.3).
F4. No pilot of ours writes to another player. A contact is passed to the Fleet Admiral.
  Goal: diplomacy has one voice.
  Changes when: approved templates exist.
F5. No new pilot and no faction without Suggi's word.
  Goal: permanent choices are Suggi's.
  Changes when: Suggi's word.
F7. Every pilot keeps 2,000 cr in its wallet.
  Goal: the weekly tax is taken from the wallet (Voidborn: 6% of the week's income, 0.75% of the ship's value); next assessment about 2026-11-16 12:00 UTC.
  Changes when: the tax is prepaid, or the rates change.
F8. No ship is idle. Every ship works, all the time, the first open route of its role's list: one that pays, or else one that trains its pilot. A turn lasts four hours; at its end the plan is set again from what the runs measured (routes/index.md).
  Goal: every ship earns or levels, and a ship born later climbs the same ladder without a hand.
  Changes when: Suggi's word; a route that loses money and trains nothing its ships need leaves the plan.
F9. A hunter fights grazers of 100 hull or less, one hunter per place, and flees under 60% hull or when a ship joins the fight.
  Goal: no ship lost to a hunt.
  Changes when: a hull is tested against bigger prey and its route says so.
TURN
T3. 2026-11-15 15:52 to 19:52 UTC. The plan of routes/plan.json: every pilot flies the two-mission circuit once; drones hunt at the grazing grounds; scouts read each Voidborn system again every half hour; every other ship mines for skill, ore into storage.
  Done when: each route of the plan has its measured figure in routes/index.md and the plan of the next turn is set from them.
EVERY ADMIRAL
Order: each turn, read this entry, the state of your ships (the fleet folder of the unit's data), the figures of the routes they fly (routes/index.md) and their last run logs. Report what your ships did, earned and cost, what failed, and one proposal that would raise your measure, with its numbers.
Limits: F1 holds. You fly no ship, start no runner and change no file of routes/ or fleet/. Reading is free: the data folder, and calls through the gate that only read, for your own ships. A proposal goes into Suggestions of your session entry and into your report; what cannot wait a turn goes to queue.log with @Unity. The shared skill fleet-play says how each kind of work is done.
ZERO, Mining (the miner- ships)
Order: find mined goods that pay. From what the fields of our space hold (the scouting files) and what our stations bid for or make things from (the market files, the catalog's recipes), name the one chain most worth a test with one ship: what to mine, where, what to make of it, where to sell it, and the credits per ship-hour you expect.
Measure: credits per ship-hour of the mining routes (today below zero: common ore sells for 1 to 4 cr); the Mining level of your pilots.
MERCURY, Trade (the trader- ships)
Order: find a trade that holds. From the order books the census saves every half hour, name the price gaps between two of our stations that held in two reads in a row and cover fuel and the 1% sales tax, and the station-need missions on the boards that goods of ours could fill. Propose one circuit route with a price cap and a price floor.
Measure: credits per ship-hour from buying and selling (today: no such route).
APOLLO, Logistics (the hauler- ships)
Order: know what the fleet owns and where. List the goods in our holds and in storage by station, and say for each where it sells or what it feeds. Work out the fuel a starter burns per jump and on each route of the plan. Propose one hauling circuit that turns stored goods into credits, or a cheaper home station for a route.
Measure: credits recovered from stored goods; fuel per ship-hour of the fleet's routes.
APOPHIS, Military (the drone- ships)
Order: make hunting pay more and lose nothing. From the hunt runs and the herd counts (the wildlife files), give for each hunting place the kills and credits per hunter-hour, the damage taken and how the herd changed. Say which place to add or to rest, and whether a railgun per hunter pays for itself. Name the armed pilots seen at our hunting grounds (players/index.md).
Measure: credits per hunter-hour; ships lost, which stays 0.
ORACLE, Intel (the scout- ships)
Order: keep the fleet's picture fresh and find what we cannot see yet. Check that every Voidborn system was read within the last hour (the scouting, market, missions and wildlife files) and that the intel files and their indexes are current. Name the three places beyond Voidborn space most worth one scout: the route, its risk and what we would look for there. Sending it is Suggi's decision (F3).
Measure: the age of the oldest system read; intel files added or corrected.

